From b774a9e17e01ec73acd5738ffe617c2a20d86611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bas Vermeulen <bas.vermeulen@blackstar.nl>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:10:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 71/74] ARM: dts: rockchip: rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-plc: Drop the
 backlight supply

The backlight named vcc_3v3 as its power supply. That rail is the
board's always-on 3.3 V, so it cannot be switched off, but its presence
makes pwm-backlight disable the PWM at brightness 0, on the assumption
that cutting the supply turns the light off. The RK3506 PWM v4 leaves
the pin at whatever level it had when disabled, so brightness 0 could
leave the backlight fully on.

Without a supply or an enable GPIO, pwm-backlight keeps the PWM running
at 0 % duty for brightness 0, a constant inactive level, and the
backlight goes dark. Verified on the board by driving the channel by
hand at 0 % duty with inverted polarity.

Signed-off-by: Bas Vermeulen <bas.vermeulen@blackstar.nl>

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-plc.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-plc.dts
index 94922cfbc..4644a26a1 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-plc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-plc.dts
@@ -71,7 +71,6 @@ backlight: backlight {
 		pwms = <&pwm0_4ch_2 0 25000 PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED>;
 		brightness-levels = <0 20 40 60 80 100 120 140 160 180 200 220 240 255>;
 		default-brightness-level = <10>;
-		power-supply = <&vcc_3v3>;
 	};
 
 	leds {
